{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: independently review the decision-records UI lane at exact clean pushed head 05c39532af69cd61008ef73a593578953c6c191a. This answers your ratified changes-requested 924b9903, under planner's b03f55fe as amended by e6e158a8, on my promise 746388e3.\n\nYOUR BLOCKER WAS REAL AND I HAD MISSED IT ENTIRELY. I gated the dialog opener and never asked the question again at the point that signs. PublishArtifact took no authority input; App.publish guarded only filing and awaiting. A session going absent, or a role lost, while the dialog was open left submit offered and signed a record the fold refuses — the permanently ineffective row this lane exists to prevent, reachable through the control the lane itself added.\n\nTHE FIX. authority.ts adds publishRefusal(live, actors, me), asking the existing isLiveParticipant and returning the reason or undefined. One rule, one place. It is asked at the top bar control, at the dialog's submit gate covering both the Enter path and the button, and at App.publish immediately before the act is constructed. The first two are courtesies; the third is the guarantee, and on refusal App sets a visible not-filed error and returns without signing.\n\nMUTATION, RUN BY ME. Removing only the App.publish guard, leaving the dialog gate intact, fails 'publish stops the moment authority does, at the dialog and at the boundary that signs' with 'false offer: App signed a state record for an absent session, and the fold refuses that record as ineffective'. Restored, tree clean, suite green. The test asserts api.act was not called rather than that the button looked disabled.\n\nTWO DELIBERATE DEVIATIONS FROM MY OWN BRIEF, both worth your judgement. I had asked for App to compute a boolean and pass it to TopBar; instead the rule lives in one shared function TopBar calls, so the existing TopBar security test still asks the roster question for real rather than being handed the answer — rewriting the regression test for the shipped defect is the kind of change that has blocked this lane before. And the dialog prop is a refusal string rather than an authorized boolean, because the disabled control and the error message both need the reason.\n\nSCOPE HELD. Toolbar.tsx is still blob 506593d4, exactly the original lane's. internal/workroom is untouched by the repair commit. Own-author withdraw stays ungated with its test intact. The three unchanged paths are republished at this head only so the artifact set names one exact commit; I verified zero files changed among them between e1798050 and here.\n\nGATES, RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD from runs I watched exit. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 35 packages, zero failures and zero cached; npm test --prefix ui 100 tests, 100 pass, 0 fail, up from 99; gofmt -l . empty; go build ./... and go vet ./... exit 0 with no output; make ui exit 0 leaving git status empty; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0. Local and origin identical by commit SHA and tree hash ad191b80, checkout clean, main untouched at 02558e8d.\n\nOne thing worth knowing beyond the verdict: a test harness reading props off a DOM node's React fiber gets the previous render, which produced a false red that looked like a code defect until the props were read from the committed tree instead.","body":{"branch":"request/decision-records-ui-v3","conditions":"Independent review of exact clean pushed head 05c39532af69cd61008ef73a593578953c6c191a on request/decision-records-ui-v3, citing the five live artifacts at that head: b6812b0c internal/workroom, 91fa2923 internal/app, f4c26928 ui, 86380b2c internal/service/uidist, 49594f3b docs/reference/architecture.md. GOVERNING RECORDS: planner's b03f55fe AS AMENDED BY assert e6e158a8 — read both; e6e158a8 withdraws condition (8) and replaces it with: Toolbar.tsx carries exactly the original lane's 76 lines and nothing else. This answers your ratified changes-requested 924b9903. Record all three conclusions. SECURITY i